# The repository already has a consistent split, and this file exists to keep it
# that way rather than to change anything:
#
#   project sources (.cpp/.h/.sln/.vcxproj/.bat)  -> CRLF   (MSVC / repo convention)
#   vendored trees  (imgui/, kiero/)              -> LF     (byte-identical to upstream)
#   docs and CI     (*.md, *.yml)                 -> LF
#
# Deliberately NO `* text=auto` and no broad `eol=` rules: those would renormalise
# the vendored LF files on the next checkout and destroy the property that imgui/
# and kiero/ are byte-for-byte identical to their upstream releases, which is what
# makes them re-syncable with a plain file copy.

# cmd.exe misparses LF-only batch files (labels and multi-line blocks in
# particular), so pin the one file type where the line ending is functional.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Vendored third-party code: store and check out exactly as committed.
imgui/** -text
kiero/** -text

# Binary assets - never diff or normalise these.
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.dll binary
*.pdb binary
*.lib binary
